{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking","id":139347,"title":"Surmounting the Daysleep = Indefinite waking?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-16T08:40:51-07:00","id":139347,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Surmounting the Daysleep = Indefinite waking?","content":"Do Vampires need sleep for anything other than healing aggravated damage or can a Dragon with Coil of the Ascendant 1: Surmounting the Daysleep wake indefinitely as long as he has Vitae to maintain Blush of Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3034-biggboss83","name":"biggboss83","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:45:49-07:00","id":139361,"title":"","content":"They need it to avoid getting the Lethargic Condition as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:47:43-07:00","id":139390,"title":"","content":"Well with Surmounting the Daysleep he has immunity to Lethargic. So yeahs, in effect he can stay awake as long as he can keep Blush of Life active. So that basically means that yeah, you can never go to sleep, but you're also using 2 vitae/24hours to keep awake... (if you also have The Warm Face)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T09:00:55-07:00","id":139398,"title":"","content":"Ah, true true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T12:07:52-07:00","id":139626,"title":"","content":"What about True Worm merit? If you no longer recover will power in sleep and can stay awake for any reason, why would you daysleep?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T15:11:38-07:00","id":139862,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the replies. I thought maybe I was missing something but it really seems you can stay awake indefinitely with this coil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3034-biggboss83","name":"biggboss83","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T17:38:40-07:00","id":140055,"title":"","content":"There are some powers that require sleep like healing aggravated damage. Otherwise, they can stay awake indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:15:54-07:00","id":140263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=139626#post139626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about True Worm merit? If you no longer recover will power in sleep and can stay awake for any reason, why would you daysleep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Healing damage for example... <br /> Also, I bet that not sleeping for long amount of time is a breaking point, since after all, you're even forgoing sleep...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:24:51-07:00","id":140265,"title":"","content":"It would take a lot of Vitae. Blush of Life is only active for a scene. I think there's a ritual or something that makes it last longer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-17-2014, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T22:34:20-07:00","id":140271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=140265#post140265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would take a lot of Vitae. Blush of Life is only active for a scene. I think there's a ritual or something that makes it last longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned above, the second dot in the same coil allows your Blush of Life to last for 24hours... so no, it wouldn't take much, just one more vitae a /night","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T01:53:28-07:00","id":140341,"title":"","content":"Also if you're always awake and busy, you can't regain willpower point by sleeping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/822-daemonchrno","name":"DaemonChrno","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar822_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"118"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:41:21-07:00","id":140418,"title":"","content":"You don't regain willpower from sleeping anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:49:30-07:00","id":140424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>solomon birch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=140418#post140418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't regain willpower from sleeping anymore.*</div> </div> </div> </div>*as a vampire.<br /> <br /> (Just adding for the sake of those less accustomed to the rules than us regulars.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:53:22-07:00","id":140427,"title":"","content":"Thanks. My mind just defaults to vampire rules.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T19:56:55-07:00","id":850936,"title":"","content":"High jacking. <br /> <br /> Are you sure you need to keep blush going all day? You only roll once at dawn and if you pass you stay awake all day. <br /> <br /> So if you blush at dawn and you don't have to roll, do you just stay awake? <br /> <br /> <br /> The wording says. As long as you benefit from blush you don't need to roll and you don't get lethargic <br /> <br /> daysleep says you only need to roll at dawn. And once you're up, you're up unless you get lethargic. <br /> <br /> Developer thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 03-21-2016, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T21:42:10-07:00","id":850960,"title":"","content":"To be fair, it's entirely in character for the Ordo - screw sleep, you've got <i>research</i> to do. You'll take a nap if someone sets you on fire, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T21:52:43-07:00","id":850962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=850936#post850936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure you need to keep blush going all day? You only roll once at dawn and if you pass you stay awake all day.<br /> <br /> So if you blush at dawn and you don't have to roll, do you just stay awake?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Surmounting the Daysleep says &quot;So long as she benefits from the blush of life (p. 90) the Dragon need not roll to resist her daily slumber, nor will she gain the Lethargic Condition (p. 305) for remaining active during the day.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Daysleep rules say, &quot;To resist sleep, make a Stamina + Resolve roll. If successful, the vampire remains alert and active, but she gains the Lethargic Condition (see p. 305).&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't get the &quot;remains alert and active&quot; status until you succeed at the roll, and you don't get to make the roll until you no longer have the Blush of Life. So, if you have it on for one hour at dawn, you'd be fine and wouldn't need to roll anything at dawn, then one hour later, you'd roll normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T00:15:28-07:00","id":851000,"title":"","content":"Why is the Dragon spend 2 vitae a day to stay awake? I understand the 1 Vitae fo the day, but if they never go into daysleep why do they have to spend 1Vitae for waking from daysleep if they neven went to sleep in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T03:08:46-07:00","id":851045,"title":"","content":"To keep Blush of Life active. Barring the use of other abilities, it only lasts one scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T03:56:39-07:00","id":851056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851000#post851000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Dragon spend 2 vitae a day to stay awake? I understand the 1 Vitae fo the day, but if they never go into daysleep why do they have to spend 1Vitae for waking from daysleep if they neven went to sleep in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they're assuming that you have to spend one vitae at sunset no matter what, which was the case in first edition. I can find no such rule in second.<br /> <br /> It seems the mounting penalty from lethargic has largely replaced it, as you simply continue to wind down until you next sleep. Since the 24hr blush of life from this coil surmounts that, it would appear that this is sufficient to keep the vampire going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T04:33:24-07:00","id":851066,"title":"","content":"Here's the part where I think that a Dragon might not want to Surmount the Daysleep all the time. Boredom<br /> <br /> Sure, you can avoid sleep. Sure, you can walk into sunlight now, in brief stretches, but it still effing HURTS. So, you don't want to do it all the time. No matter your Potency or Humanity, you don't want to be outside for an hour in daylight. You can have every Scale and Coil in the Mystery of the Ascended, and you'll still be taking damage from sunlight exposure once every 10 minutes. Great in a pinch, but not exactly something that will be every day. <br /> <br /> So, as the years stretch on... what do you DO during the daylight hours? Remember, ennui is a theme in Vampire. They get bored as they get old. Sure, its easy to theorycraft all the nice new hobbies you could pick up after all that time, all the books you can read, but that's really not sustainable long term. Cabin fever is still a thing with vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T05:50:27-07:00","id":851092,"title":"","content":"It's still a fantastic way to use up your time if you are a crafting/mental oriented character. Can't go outside during a day, but don't have to sleep? Utilize that space to build equipment, investigate clues, and do other time consuming things that would be impractical during action scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T06:15:55-07:00","id":851103,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I appreciate the feedback. <br /> <br /> Run out of vitae to stay awake all day, you face plant! Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T08:50:42-07:00","id":851167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851066#post851066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the part where I think that a Dragon might not want to Surmount the Daysleep all the time. Boredom<br /> <br /> Sure, you can avoid sleep. Sure, you can walk into sunlight now, in brief stretches, but it still effing HURTS. So, you don't want to do it all the time. No matter your Potency or Humanity, you don't want to be outside for an hour in daylight. You can have every Scale and Coil in the Mystery of the Ascended, and you'll still be taking damage from sunlight exposure once every 10 minutes. Great in a pinch, but not exactly something that will be every day. <br /> <br /> So, as the years stretch on... what do you DO during the daylight hours? Remember, ennui is a theme in Vampire. They get bored as they get old. Sure, its easy to theorycraft all the nice new hobbies you could pick up after all that time, all the books you can read, but that's really not sustainable long term. Cabin fever is still a thing with vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your point, but wanted to point out that a dragon with Sun's Forgotten Kiss can actually be in the sun as long as they want without taking damage, if they spend enough Vitae to lower their effective Blood Potency to 1 and then bundle up so only their eyes are uncovered. Though, depending on how high the vampire's Blood Potency is, that could cost a *lot* of Vitae - certainly too much to reliably make this an every day thing. More like something you do sparingly, when there's a real need to go outside for extended periods during the day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T09:18:48-07:00","id":851179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851167#post851167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with your point, but wanted to point out that a dragon with Sun's Forgotten Kiss can actually be in the sun as long as they want without taking damage, if they spend enough Vitae to lower their effective Blood Potency to 1 and then bundle up so only their eyes are uncovered. Though, depending on how high the vampire's Blood Potency is, that could cost a *lot* of Vitae - certainly too much to reliably make this an every day thing. More like something you do sparingly, when there's a real need to go outside for extended periods during the day.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hm? Ah, yes, I forgot that. I was looking at the Coil where its said BP 1 at lowest, and forgot that you could go lower with lots of cover. So, I suppose it is still viable between the Humanity and BP dropping powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T09:20:59-07:00","id":851183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851092#post851092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a fantastic way to use up your time if you are a crafting/mental oriented character. Can't go outside during a day, but don't have to sleep? Utilize that space to build equipment, investigate clues, and do other time consuming things that would be impractical during action scenes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, once in a while if you already have a purpose in mind. Every day avoiding sleep? That I can't see as much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:03:28-07:00","id":952920,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I don't mean to resurrect and old thread, but I have a question about something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851167#post851167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with your point, but wanted to point out that a dragon with Sun's Forgotten Kiss can actually be in the sun as long as they want without taking damage, if they spend enough Vitae to lower their effective Blood Potency to 1 and then bundle up so only their eyes are uncovered. Though, depending on how high the vampire's Blood Potency is, that could cost a *lot* of Vitae - certainly too much to reliably make this an every day thing. More like something you do sparingly, when there's a real need to go outside for extended periods during the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How does that work? I know of the powers to reduce the blood potency, even the one to increases humanity levels when dealing with sunlight. But what about this being able to stay out in the sun, no issues, if you are completely covered? This was something I always wanted to do with a character. Had a suit designed kind of like the one from Repo: The Genetic Opera. High quality material, but with cameras on the outside. Basically (with today's technology) it would be like using the Oculus Rift and seeing outside the suit with 3D goggles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:15:01-07:00","id":952921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=952920#post952920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't mean to resurrect and old thread, but I have a question about something.<br /> <br /> How does that work? I know of the powers to reduce the blood potency, even the one to increases humanity levels when dealing with sunlight. But what about this being able to stay out in the sun, no issues, if you are completely covered? This was something I always wanted to do with a character. Had a suit designed kind of like the one from Repo: The Genetic Opera. High quality material, but with cameras on the outside. Basically (with today's technology) it would be like using the Oculus Rift and seeing outside the suit with 3D goggles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 102: &quot;A character can avoid damage from sunlight only with complete coverage from its rays. If she only exposes her eyes, for example to run for shelter, consider her Blood Potency one step lower on the chart.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if you have Blood Potency 1, either naturally or by using Sun's Forgotten Kiss, covering everything but your eyes reduces your effective Blood Potency to 0, and the damage frequency on the chart for Blood Potency 0 is &quot;-&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T19:30:45-07:00","id":952929,"title":"","content":"Awesome. That sounds familiar, just forgot about it I guess. Gogo ninja outfits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:52:53-07:00","id":953437,"title":"","content":"And snow days!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T06:29:30-07:00","id":953790,"title":"","content":"It's useful when you imagine it from the character's perspective: you can get up to more mundane chores, hobbies, and research during the day (reading an interesting book, painting, writing up architectural plans, writing) - and devote every night to being social and partaking in kindred society. You effectively have more time to complete more mundane activities and can devote more time toward social activities. The other benefit is your ability to invite people over during the day; this gives you a much better flexibility in allying with mortals, creating better social networks. It allows you greater flexibility and reliability when sustaining your masquerade.<br /> <br /> You're also capable of wrapping yourself up and paying an enemy a visit during the day.<br /> <br /> It might also surprise enemies who visit your haven during the day to find that you're still perfectly awake and active and able to defend yourself - the fact you can garb yourself and escape your haven if its suddenly firebombed is another positive.<br /> <br /> The reality is Hunters need to strike Vampires during the day to stand a chance against them, because Vampires can absolutely maul them in regard to taking damage, healing damage, using supernatural powers, and buffing themselves up with blood (on top of whatever other defences they have in the form of retainers). Attacking during daylight hours is an absolute must - because even if you overpower a Vampire during night, they're just as capable of running away without any problem (sunlight is needed to stop them from fleeing and allows you to flee if you're about to die, as well). If it's night and things simply aren't going as planned, you're far more capable of running away in the daylight to escape the Vampire. But if it's dark out and you've managed to spur a Vampire to chase you down without any contingency, you're screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T10:02:40-07:00","id":953896,"title":"","content":"Hehe...<br /> <br /> Dragon: 'You're an immortal and as such have infinite time if you are careful. I am an immortal that doesn't need to sleep, so I have twice that.' :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:32:03-07:00","id":953929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851066#post851066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the part where I think that a Dragon might not want to Surmount the Daysleep all the time. Boredom<br /> <br /> Sure, you can avoid sleep. Sure, you can walk into sunlight now, in brief stretches, but it still effing HURTS. So, you don't want to do it all the time. No matter your Potency or Humanity, you don't want to be outside for an hour in daylight. You can have every Scale and Coil in the Mystery of the Ascended, and you'll still be taking damage from sunlight exposure once every 10 minutes. Great in a pinch, but not exactly something that will be every day.<br /> <br /> So, as the years stretch on... what do you DO during the daylight hours? Remember, ennui is a theme in Vampire. They get bored as they get old. Sure, its easy to theorycraft all the nice new hobbies you could pick up after all that time, all the books you can read, but that's really not sustainable long term. Cabin fever is still a thing with vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which I think makes for a great thematic fit for the Ordo:<i> Be careful what you wish for</i>.<br /> It looks like an awesome improvement on paper but turns out to be just another form of the curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","user":"Lepaca","date":". 08-19-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4035-lepaca","name":"Lepaca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4035_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:27:17-07:00","id":954309,"title":"","content":"Sleep also does things other than physical rest. It clears away the minor, useless details of the day and I've seen studies that it helps things get locked into long-term memory. It also seems to help (me anyway) take a new look at the problems of yesterday with a slightly different perspective which leads to new solutions, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T06:29:12-07:00","id":954339,"title":"","content":"Well, the bio-psychological effects of sleep is pretty fascinating. Yes, it does help you lock things in long term memory. It also <i>removes</i> things from memory - in fact, there's some psychologists who believe that dreams are actually are brain tossing away all that unwanted information we picked up over time. That's why suppressed memories come out in dreams - its our brain trying to heal and clean up messes. Our brain builds new connections while asleep, weakens old ones, shifts around our associations, and more. Sleep is pretty dang fascinating from a biological standpoint.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, vampires are undead, so their brain functions are kinda different. Torpor does help with the memory thing - it makes long term vampires who've frozen into bad habits into someone new and fresh and open to ideas and changes. And daysleep does help with healing, like with humans. So, its entirely possible that sleep will serve a similar function in vampires. That said, vampires don't recover willpower from sleeping, so its not like they wake up refreshed, and constant low level healing from spending vitae can function as the same memory issues. Or if the memory thing can only be acomplished via torpor. <br /> <br /> .....<br /> <br /> I have an idea for my next Dragon PC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:10:12-07:00","id":954360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954339#post954339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, vampires don't recover willpower from sleeping</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Really? Is this explicit in the corebook, or is it one of those houserules I've had for so long I'm thinking they're RAW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:39:56-07:00","id":954411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954360#post954360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, what? Really? Is this explicit in the corebook, or is it one of those houserules I've had for so long I'm thinking they're RAW?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Think it was taken out in 2E. If it wasn't there it begin with then I'm right there with you lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:05:44-07:00","id":954423,"title":"","content":"It's something that was supposed to be in the 2e book, at least according to Rose, Vampire lead. I'm going by that, which is admittedly debatable in terms of cannon or not. Take as you will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:18:51-07:00","id":954433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954423#post954423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's something that was supposed to be in the 2e book, at least according to Rose, Vampire lead. I'm going by that, which is admittedly debatable in terms of cannon or not. Take as you will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Supposed to be in as: kindred are suppose to regain willpower, or in as they are not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:36:16-07:00","id":954441,"title":"","content":"2e doesn't specify whether or not vampires regain Willpower when they sleep. Rose has confirmed that the intent is for vampires specifically not to regain Willpower when they sleep, but it got left out due to the awkward start 2e had where it was &quot;chronicle books&quot; instead of a proper second edition. I'll see if I can dig up a quote about it from her when I get the chance.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/52522-regaining-willpower?p=53362#post53362\">Here's</a> her explicitly stating the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-20-2016, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:48:27-07:00","id":954452,"title":"","content":"Ya, that's the reasoning why I thought they shouldn't regain it. Seems more of a mortal concept anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:13:02-07:00","id":954467,"title":"","content":"In light of that argument, though, makes you wonder if staying awake that long should <i>drain </i>willpower for being that exhasting, or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T10:23:27-07:00","id":954475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954467#post954467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In light of that argument, though, makes you wonder if staying awake that long should <i>drain </i>willpower for being that exhasting, or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, vampires don't regain Willpower from sleeping because their sleep isn't restful. Or sleep, technically. No rest for the wicked and all that, vampires merely go dormant when the sun comes up as part of their Bane. When a Defiant finds a way to circumvent that Bane, they aren't any less rested than those that succumb to it, because activity doesn't tire vampires and day&quot;sleep&quot; doesn't renew their energy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-20-2016, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:05:18-07:00","id":954498,"title":"","content":"Ive alwaya felt the willpower thing was silly, an additional weakness that makes little thematic sense (I disagree with &quot;theyre undead so it isnt restful cus i dunno!&quot;). They dont gain any extra way to gain wp and in games ive been in its plenty scarce to start with","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T11:57:56-07:00","id":954525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954498#post954498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They dont gain any extra way to gain wp and in games ive been in its plenty scarce to start with</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they do. A human's Vice only gives him one Willpower and his Virtue only gives him all Willpower. A vampire's Mask and Dirge each give her both. Each is like a Virtue/Vice set, and vampires get two of them. On top of that, vampires get Willpower for interacting with their Touchstones. Humans can get Willpower for interacting with True Friends, but that's a 3-dot Merit approximating a benefit every vampire gets for free, and can get more of for 1 Merit dot a pop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T12:18:57-07:00","id":954539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954525#post954525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure they do. A human's Vice only gives him one Willpower and his Virtue only gives him all Willpower. A vampire's Mask and Dirge each give her both. Each is like a Virtue/Vice set, and vampires get two of them. On top of that, vampires get Willpower for interacting with their Touchstones. Humans can get Willpower for interacting with True Friends, but that's a 3-dot Merit approximating a benefit every vampire gets for free, and can get more of for 1 Merit dot a pop.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was comparing more to other supernaturals, to be clear. Werewolves have the same allotment of double-acting Blood/Bone anchors and touchstones (they have more of them, even), and Mages, while they use Virtue/Vice, have so many different ways to regain willpower through magic it doesn't matter that they lack touchstones. Both still regain willpower from sleeping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T16:29:41-07:00","id":954676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=851056#post851056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they're assuming that you have to spend one vitae at sunset no matter what, which was the case in first edition. I can find no such rule in second.<br /> <br /> It seems the mounting penalty from lethargic has largely replaced it, as you simply continue to wind down until you next sleep. Since the 24hr blush of life from this coil surmounts that, it would appear that this is sufficient to keep the vampire going.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would realy like a developer to yes or no this because if true it would mean a vampire who got far enough north or south at the right time of year could stay up indefinitely. Getting in effect free brush of life sounds ok for a Dragon but 6 months awake for 1 rat is a tad to far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:52:46-07:00","id":954756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954676#post954676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would realy like a developer to yes or no this because if true it would mean a vampire who got far enough north or south at the right time of year could stay up indefinitely. Getting in effect free brush of life sounds ok for a Dragon but 6 months awake for 1 rat is a tad to far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, who cares about developer intent in that case? It's obvious you don't want it to work that way in your games, so just go ahead and rule that it doesn't work that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:53:41-07:00","id":954785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954676#post954676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting in effect free brush of life sounds ok for a Dragon but 6 months awake for 1 rat is a tad to far.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a story-oriented game, you're just choosing to tell the story of a vampire who lives in a place where there's more night. They may have avoided the need for Daysleep, at least for half a year, but it's not as if suddenly there's no challenges or obstacles or dramatic situations you could throw at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-20-2016, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:44:20-07:00","id":954828,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;6 months of night and 6 months of day&quot; thing is pretty overstated anyway. Granted, north of the Arctic Circle or south of the Antarctic Circle you'll get periods of 24 hours or more without the sun rising near the winter solstice and 24 hours or more without the sun setting near the summer solstice. But it's only in very close proximity to the poles that you get true 6 month days and 6 month nights. And there really arent any humans living that far north or south to feed on. Like, granted, you won't have to spend Vitae to wake up so the only thing you'll be spending it on during those 6 months is healing, Physical Intensity, and Disciplines. But what are you even doing there that whole time? 6 months active with no one but penguins to talk to? You'd go Draughur from the isolation. I could maybe see one ancient, deranged Gangrel shutting herself off from the world to go live as a polar bear for eternity, but talk about a boring game of Vampire the Requiem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-21-2016, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:48:09-07:00","id":954830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954828#post954828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &amp;quot;6 months of night and 6 months of day&amp;quot; thing is pretty overstated anyway. Granted, north of the Arctic Circle or south of the Antarctic Circle you'll get periods of 24 hours or more without the sun rising near the winter solstice and 24 hours or more without the sun setting near the summer solstice. But it's only in very close proximity to the poles that you get true 6 month days and 6 month nights. And there really arent any humans living that far north or south to feed on. Like, granted, you won't have to spend Vitae to wake up so the only thing you'll be spending it on during those 6 months is healing, Physical Intensity, and Disciplines. But what are you even doing there that whole time? 6 months active with no one but penguins to talk to? You'd go Draughur from the isolation. I could maybe see one ancient, deranged Gangrel shutting herself off from the world to go live as a polar bear for eternity, but talk about a boring game of Vampire the Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they are making a penguin army?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T22:50:39-07:00","id":954831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954830#post954830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they are making a penguin army?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/adventuretimewithfinnandjake/images/f/f0/S6e20_Ice_King_and_penguins.png/revision/latest?cb=20141128053643\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T06:16:28-07:00","id":954924,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that we should really focus less on getting official rules, and looking at all of this as a giant source of potential plot hooks. Official rules just bog down games, while room to make individual rulings help promote individual styles and stories. Can an Ordo Dracul Ascendant never sleep? Are there any drawbacks? Lets have characters experiment and find out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:43:41-07:00","id":955099,"title":"","content":"By an astounding coincidence, the latitudes that get 6 months of darkness are also the ones sufficiently cold that you need to spend a vitae every 24 hours to stop yourself freezing solid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:43:28-07:00","id":955983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/139347-surmounting-the-daysleep-indefinite-waking?p=954756#post954756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, who cares about developer intent in that case? It's obvious you don't want it to work that way in your games, so just go ahead and rule that it doesn't work that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with it working that way as it cuts the feeding needs of the biker dragon day hunter I plan on making some day in half (before healing) but knowing how the developers thought it would work is always interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}